 "notes": "First page of Table XV Part II (B) Tri and poly-lingualism (printed page 256). Stub headed 'Taluk.'; braces: 'Jammu and Kashmir State' (10 mother tongues), then 'Jammu Province' (Dogri, Kashmiri on this leaf; block continues on leaf 267 without a label). Subsidiary headers printed 'Dogri. (B)', 'Panjabi (C)', 'Kashmiri. (D)'; recorded as Dogri/Panjabi/Kashmiri. The letters B/C/D are used in the remarks on later pages. Remarks are transcribed as printed, including '2197males' with no space. Letters with broken type (e.g. 'an'l' for 'and', 'speakin;' for 'speaking') are given as the intended word. Every row's remark counts agree with the figures: males/females speaking 3 languages = sum of pair counts, and each subsidiary column equals the sum of the pairs that include it. No printed column numbers."
